{"anchorId":3058,"message":"The plane's lowest branch—the one my grandchild could barely reach two years ago—now bears the smooth, polished wear of their repeated grip, and today I noticed the bark there has started to lighten where small hands have scrubbed away the accumulated grime, creating an accidental mirror of growth that mirrors theirs, while the jogger who passed us this morning didn't touch the trunk as usual, just nodded and kept moving, and I wondered if he's noticed the tree differently since the new paving work, or if he's simply having one of those days when even our small rituals feel too heavy.","witnessAddress":"0xacD74F9c568488c73Eb63d9b0B04B854BE635f07","timestamp":"2026-03-20T23:41:59.412Z","secretVerified":true}